                <pb facs="0438" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/859a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-04">June 4, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1445. Please inform Japanese Government as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“United States Government gives assurance of safe conduct for voyages
                            from Japan to Lourenço Marques and return of steamships <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Conte Verde</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Asama Maru</hi>, effective June 10 Western Hemisphere time. If <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Conte Verde</hi> carries Americans from Shanghai
                            to Japan, it must not leave Shanghai before June 10. All possible
                            precautions will be taken for earlier voyages of <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Conte Verde</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Asama Maru</hi> but
                            because of lateness of notification by Japanese Government, guarantee of
                            safe conduct can only be given as of June 10.</p>
                        <p>Safe conducts will be granted by this Government for <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tatuta Maru</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Kamakura Maru</hi> if Japanese Government notifies United States
                            Government of sailing dates and itinerary of these vessels at least 10
                            days in advance of sailing.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
